# FINXIA Capital - Deployment Configuration

## Application Type
FastAPI backend serving Next.js static build

## Architecture
- **Backend**: FastAPI (port 8001) serves both API endpoints and Next.js static files
- **Frontend**: Next.js 15 SSG (Static Site Generation)
- **Database**: MongoDB Atlas (managed by Emergent in production)

## Build Process
1. Backend installs Python dependencies from requirements.txt
2. Next.js builds static site to `/app/frontend-nextjs/out/`
3. FastAPI serves static files from `/out` directory

## Production Endpoints
- **Static pages**: served by FastAPI at root `/`
- **API endpoints**: `/api/health`, `/api/contact`, etc.
- **Health check**: `GET /api/health`

## Environment Variables (Production)
- `MONGO_URL`: Provided by Emergent (MongoDB Atlas connection string)
- `DB_NAME`: Database name for MongoDB
- `CORS_ORIGINS`: "*" (allows all origins)
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL`: Will be set to production domain

## Pre-deployment Checklist
✅ Next.js build completes successfully
✅ Backend serves static files from /out directory
✅ API health check responds with 200
✅ All pages return 200 status code
✅ CORS configured for production
✅ MongoDB connection uses environment variable (not hardcoded)

## Known Configuration
- Backend binds to 0.0.0.0:8001
- Frontend static files served via FastAPI
- No separate frontend server needed in production
